# The journey's PINNED brief_pack versions, one per pack path. Requires a
# preceding `journey_scope(journey_id)` CTE naming the journey to read (bound
# directly from a journey_id bind, or resolved from a dispatch).
#
# DOCTRINE — a pinned read NEVER consults deprecation. A journey pins its pack
# versions at create time precisely so multiple guide versions run actively
# side by side; a later re-ingest deprecating a pack version MUST NOT change
# what this journey resolves. Deprecation events gate browse/catalog and
# new-journey attachment ONLY. The 2026-06-01 filter here (`ld.to_level_id IS
# NULL`, commit 5eb5649f) silently nulled out every pre-re-ingest journey's
# pack: the computed-output producer, the /stages + /steps DONE rollups, the
# dispatch-ready gates and the journey brief reads all went empty the moment a
# sync deprecated the pinned version. Do not reintroduce it.
#
# DISTINCT ON (path): dedup of the historical stacked-pin corruption (old
# backfills inserted multiple versions of one pack path onto a journey —
# Issue #505's legitimate half). Newest pinned row wins, deterministically
# (UUIDv7 id breaks created_at ties). This dedups among the journey's OWN
# pinned rows; it never resolves "latest by path" across the catalog.
#
# No trailing comma — callers appending further CTEs add a leading comma
# after the compose call (same convention as shared/journey_chain.sqlc).
journey_packs AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT ON (bpvo.path_id) bpack.id AS brief_pack_id
    FROM journey_scope js
    JOIN rev.journey_brief_packs jbp ON jbp.journey_id = js.journey_id
    JOIN rev.brief_packs bpack ON bpack.id = jbp.brief_pack_id
    JOIN rev.versioned_objects bpvo ON bpvo.id = bpack.versioned_object_id
    ORDER BY bpvo.path_id, bpvo.created_at DESC, bpvo.id DESC
)
